senses.gloss:
darśana, nt., once m. (Skt. nt., not in these senses; cf. ˚nā),
(1) nt., = dṛṣṭi, false, heretical view: tasyedaṃ darśanaṃ abhūt, śubhāśubhānāṃ karmāṇāṃ phalam nāstīti niścayaḥ Mv 〔i.178.11〕 (vs);
(2) once m. (= Pali dassana, nt., in sippa-d˚), exhibition (of skill in arts or exercises): kumāro … darśanaṃ dāsyati Mv 〔ii.73.18〕; 〔74.4, 7〕; kumāreṇa … darśano dinnaḥ 〔75.18〕; darśana-śatāni vartanti 〔iii.57.9〕, hundreds of exhibitions (as entertainments at a festival).
